[Music]  to celebrate hispanic heritage month  we're going to do it one of the best  ways we know how and that's by taking a  look at five essential spanish language  films  on the ketchup with the help of film  critic and journalist monica castillo we  curated a list of the 110 essential  spanish language movies at  rottentomatoes.com and it is filled with  some classic favorites  festival winners and even a few oscar  contenders  we're looking at the top five on that  list starting with a short film from  1965 called simon of the desert now this  venice film festival winner is a hundred  percent fresh and is about a deeply  religious man living in the fourth  century simon  who climbs the stone column in the  middle of the desert and prays for six  years six weeks and six days while the  devil tries to seduce him to calm down  i can totally relate and coming in at  number four is the 2001 film  la cienega it is a certified fresh  dramedy from highly decorated  argentinian director  lucretia martell and this one follows a  group of families having summer vacation  in a rural country house in argentina  with the critics calling it  dense yet impressively focused and a  disquieting look at domestic  dissatisfaction  [Music]  number three on our list is 1999's all  about my mother from acclaimed writer  director pedro almodovar  this certified fresh film is about a  heartbroken mother who goes in search of  her son's father now a trans woman  after her son is tragically killed in a  car accident with a cast that includes  cecilia roth and penelope cruz  this drama won both an oscar and a  golden globe for best foreign language  film  finding its way to number two on this  list is of course 2006 pans labyrinth  it was written and directed by the  guillermo del toro and follows the young  stepdaughter of a sadistic army officer  as she escapes into an eerie but  captivating fantasy world this film  which critics call a  spellbinding fable that's like alice in  wonderland but for grownups is really  all about the visuals considering it  picked up oscars for cinematography art  direction  and makeup and finally number one on our  list of the 110  essential spanish language movies is  2018's roma  this drama was shot on location in  mexico city and is heavily based on  writer director alfonso cuadron's  real-life nanny when he was a child in  the early 1970s  smartly released on netflix this film  became the streaming service's first  film to be nominated for best picture  and ended up taking home gold statues  for directing foreign language film  and cinematography  alright friends those are the top five  in our list but of course let us know  what your favorite spanish language film  is in the comments and be sure  to head on over to runtomatos.com if you  want to check out the full list  and for more discussion and celebration  during hispanic heritage month come find  me in our fan group on facebook it is  muy caliente  and if you don't want to miss out on any  future episodes of this show be sure to  hit that subscribe button and  notification bell so you're covered  there  and as always muchas gracias for  watching the ketchup my name's nas perez  and hasta luego adios  [Music]  you

